// The workspace the two Aletheia Go modules are developed in.
//
// The loader that reads spreadsheets is a module of its own, ./excel, so that
// excelize and what it brings with it are optional to a consumer who wants the
// core binding alone.
//
// The replace below is what lets a change to the core module reach the Excel
// module without a release. The use directive alone does not: it registers the
// module for the workspace and leaves version resolution to the require, which
// names the last release, so Go would go looking for it on the network. The
// replace is written here rather than in that module's own file because a
// relative path written there would travel with the module. It names the same
// version the require does, a version-specific replace matching nothing when
// the two drift apart.
//
// This file is not part of the bundle a release builds, which carries the core
// module's files alone, and a consumer of either module never sees it.
go 1.24.0

toolchain go1.24.6

use (
	.
	./excel
)

replace github.com/aletheia-automotive/aletheia-go/v5 v5.0.0 => ./
